<h2>Conservative workflow before any write-capable operation</h2><ol>
<li>Identify the exact car, system and service event that may justify the procedure.</li>
<li>Preserve the original diagnostic and module-communication evidence.</li>
<li>Consult vehicle-specific manufacturer instructions before selecting the command.</li>
<li>Confirm the chosen tool's actual ECU/function coverage, license and interface.</li>
<li>Document electrical, mechanical and operator safety prerequisites.</li>
<li>Stop if any required prerequisite or procedure remains unverified.</li>
<li>Use a qualified operator for brake, steering, suspension, high-voltage, programming or other high-risk work.</li>
<li>After an approved procedure, keep the original report, completion record and required follow-up results.</li>
</ol>